Q: Display problem using UnevaluatedExpr in Sympy with python A: <p>Override just the <code>UnevaluatedExpr</code> printing rule:</p>
<pre><code>from sympy import *
from sympy.printing.str import StrPrinter

class FixedStrPrinter(StrPrinter):
    def _print_UnevaluatedExpr(self, expr):
        return f&quot;({self._print(expr.args[0])})&quot;

def pprint_fixed(expr):
    return FixedStrPrinter().doprint(expr)

x, y = symbols('x y')
ue1 = UnevaluatedExpr(-2*x**2 + 3*x + 2)
ue2 = UnevaluatedExpr(-5*x**2 + 6*x - 7)

print(pprint_fixed(ue1 + ue2))
# (-2*x**2 + 3*x + 2) + (-5*x**2 + 6*x - 7)
</code></pre>

Q: Is ResizeObserver API necessary or preferred in React? A: <p>This answer is correct, though it seems like there is some confusion about how useEffect works.  The question seems to imply that the dependency array in useEffect is somehow statefully watching everything in the array for a change.  But, useEffects dependency array is used to tell react what stateful variables the callback in useEffect is dependent on.  So, if <code>const statefulVar = useState([]);</code> is referenced in the dependency array, then the useEffect will be re-run when that state is updated.  But <code>element.clientHeight</code> is not wrapped in reacts useState(), therefore, nothing will be triggering the useEffect to be re-run.</p>
<p><code>ResizeObserver</code> on the other hand, will run a callback on every resize the browser performs.</p>
<p>If you have multiple things in the useEffect dependency array, you can update a stateful variable <code>height</code> on every resize, and then have a useEffect with the <code>height</code> variable in the dependency array, if thats the only thing the useEffect is dependent on, I would just put the callback in the useEffect in the <code>ResizeObserver</code> callback instead.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const [size, setSize] = useState({});

const observer = new ResizeObserver((entries) =&gt; {
    for (const entry of entries) {
        if (entry.contentBoxSize) {
            setSize(entry.contentBoxSize);
        }
    }
});

observer.observe(document.querySelector('#myContainer'));
// observer.disconnect() when component is not rendered.


useEffect(() =&gt; {
    // calculating something
    // updating on every size change
},[size]);

useEffect(() =&gt; {
    // calculating something
    // updating only when the component is re-rendered since there is nothing triggering react to re-run the callback.
    // No different than leaving the dependency array as []
},[ref?.current.clientHeight]);
</code></pre>

Q: How to use tailwind css code in simple html file which is used in react A: <p>According to the Documents located <a href="https://tailwindcss.com/docs/installation/play-cdn" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://tailwindcss.com/docs/installation/play-cdn</a></p>
<p>Below is using the CDN in plain HTML and the second example below has PHP with the HTML. Use the code snippet in the second example and it will have you up and running in 2 seconds.</p>
<pre><code>

&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;
  &lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;script src=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tailwindcss/browser@4&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;/head&gt;
  &lt;body&gt;
    &lt;h1 class=&quot;text-3xl font-bold underline&quot;&gt;
      Hello world!
    &lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;

&lt;!-- top without PHP  -- bottom with PHP  --&gt;

&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;script src=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tailwindcss/browser@4&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;My PHP + Tailwind Page&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body class=&quot;bg-gray-100 min-h-screen&quot;&gt;

  &lt;div class=&quot;container mx-auto p-6&quot;&gt;
    &lt;h1 class=&quot;text-4xl font-bold text-blue-700 underline mb-6&quot;&gt;
      Hello from PHP + Tailwind v4!
    &lt;/h1&gt;

    &lt;?php
    // ← Your normal PHP code goes here
    $name = &quot;NAME&quot;;
    $current_time = date(&quot;F j, Y \a\\t g:i A&quot;);
    ?&gt;

    &lt;p class=&quot;text-lg text-gray-700&quot;&gt;
      Welcome back, &lt;strong class=&quot;text-indigo-600&quot;&gt;&lt;?php echo htmlspecialchars($name); ?&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;!
    &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;p class=&quot;mt-4 text-sm text-gray-500&quot;&gt;
      Current time: &lt;?php echo $current_time; ?&gt;
    &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;div class=&quot;mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6&quot;&gt;
      &lt;?php for ($i = 1; $i &lt;= 6; $i++): ?&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md hover:shadow-xl transition&quot;&gt;
          &lt;h2 class=&quot;text-xl font-semibold mb-2&quot;&gt;Card &lt;?= $i ?&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
          &lt;p class=&quot;text-gray-600&quot;&gt;Some dynamic content here.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;?php endfor; ?&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
